#!/bin/sh
# Refuse to commit personal workspace state into the DISTRIBUTION repository.
#
# Why this exists: these seven paths are created by `awb init` in every fork and
# rewritten as a person works -- `.awb/workspace.json` changes its updatedAt
# after every write command. If the distribution tracks them, every fork
# conflicts on `git pull upstream main`, on files that have nothing to do with
# the update being pulled. An employee who is not fluent in git stops there, and
# that pull is the only channel shared skills travel through.
#
# They are deliberately left on disk and un-ignored so that a FORK can commit
# its own state. That is exactly what makes `git add -A`, or ticking every box
# in a git GUI, a one-gesture way to undo the separation -- which is what
# happened in 8d5ec1a.
#
# This hook is inert in a fork: it only fires when `origin` is the canonical
# distribution repository.

PERSONAL_PATHS="
.awb/workspace.json
knowledge/index.json
knowledge/providers.json
projects/index.json
relationships/index.json
user/PROFILE.md
work/artifacts/index.json
"

DISTRIBUTION_REMOTE="TolhNguyen/agent-workbench"

origin_url=$(git config --get remote.origin.url 2>/dev/null)
case "$origin_url" in
  *"$DISTRIBUTION_REMOTE"*) ;;
  *) exit 0 ;;   # Not the distribution -- this is somebody's workspace fork.
esac

# --diff-filter=d ignores deletions, so removing these paths is always allowed.
staged=$(git diff --cached --name-only --diff-filter=d)

offenders=""
for path in $PERSONAL_PATHS; do
  for entry in $staged; do
    [ "$entry" = "$path" ] && offenders="$offenders  $path
"
  done
done

[ -z "$offenders" ] && exit 0

cat <<'HEADER'
Refusing to commit: personal workspace state does not belong in the distribution.
HEADER
printf '\n%s\n' "$offenders"
cat <<'BODY'
These are created by `awb init` in each fork. Tracking them here makes every
fork conflict on `git pull upstream main`.

In GitHub Desktop or any git GUI: untick those files, then commit.

In a terminal, unstage them and commit again:

  git restore --staged .awb/workspace.json knowledge/index.json \
    knowledge/providers.json projects/index.json relationships/index.json \
    user/PROFILE.md work/artifacts/index.json

If all seven keep reappearing as changes every time you open the repository,
this clone has not excluded them, and they will keep inviting this mistake.
Add them to .git/info/exclude -- that file is local to this clone and is never
pushed, so a fork, where these files SHOULD be committed, is unaffected.

The test `the distributed repository ships no personal workspace state` in
test/cli.test.js checks the same thing, so `npm test` catches it too.
BODY

exit 1
